y a hard and solid gold  standard and importantly what true graph  is capturing sometimes might happen  before the biopsy is showing damage so  it's really important to think about how  gene expression is related in that omics  pathway that i mentioned earlier and how  these things are navigating together  finally the thing that i'll mention is  actually the false negatives so both  tests came back negative but 32 of those  tests were shown to have a biopsy proven  rejection event again we reduced that  number by half and that was really  really important but i think overall  what you can see from this venn diagram  is that when we think about biomarkers  sometimes people use metrics like npv  and ppv sensitivity specificity and then  think that they're comparing apples to  apples i think the most interesting  thing about this data as we published  this was that the overlap between the  two tests the cell free dna and the gene  expression is not a hundred percent so  the question is what is cell free dna  doing and what is the gene expression  doing because they don't overlap  so when we looked at this more closely  we we decided to drill into the idea of  the type of rejections that are  happening so again the green is going to  be a gene expression profile that's our  true graph score our blue circles are  going to be the cell free dna positives  and really it's split into three groups  it's antibody mediated rejection acr in  the left hand corner it's anim it's amr  so i'm sorry t-cell mediated rejection  in the upper left-hand corner the  antibody media rejection in the  right-hand corner and a mixture of both  acr and amr in that bottom uh quadrant  right there  and so again you know a busy slide but  let's highlight a couple of key points  here is the first point here is that  we're actually capturing a number of  different um rejections by looking at  the two types of tests you can see that  from the the true graph aspect you went  from 16 tests to 29 tests and you can  actually see that the four tests that  overlap that are highlighted here from  the cell free dna we're all captured by  our true graph test as well and this is  by changing over to a new technology  second to that you see that the 10  reduced from 19  and those were  19 tests originally that true graph  missed it has now been reduced to only  10 tests that true graph didn't capture  and it's increased the number of that  overlap from 12 to 21  and finally you can see that it's  capturing a number of the mixed  rejections within there and so really  when we think about all of these  rejections there were 103 rejections  that were in this cohort and there's  about 19 of them that both tests missed  but there's only 17 that that the gene  expression missed when we switched over  to a different technology again when we  went over to the pcr based technology  and so ultimately what you see is we  reduce that number and we're capturing  more rejections by using the true graph  pcr we did not change anything in the  cell free dna product and so it's really  important to understand that the  enhancements here that we're getting out  of this are simply because we have gone  from a microarray technology to this pcr  micro microfluidics technology  so the the last thing uh before i i hit  some some of the um other things to talk  about would be that that we what we've  done at tgi at transplant genomics is  try to increase the biomarker diagnostic  performance to a new standard and we've  utilized technology to be able to get us  there so when we first launched true  graph microarray you can see in the  orange bar on the left hand side that it  was a 48 91 percent positive and  negative predictive value respectively  the track cell free dna has very similar  performance metrics now what we  did in conjunction with northwestern  university is to publish uh data for the  very first time to show how the two  biomarkers can be complementary to each  other and so even though they have  similar npv's they're ruling out  different types of rejections  and so you can see with the c jason  paper that we increased our positive  predicted values from the 40s all the  way to the 80s by just looking at a  double positive predictive or a double  negative in their predictive values  and then in the next month or two we  looked at the true graph pcr getting it  off of the microarray technology onto  the biomark hd and enhance the positive  predictive value just a little bit more  now this is what we have overall our  commercial available product now which  is the omni graph where you get the true  graph pcr plus track in this in one two  that in one report is now we have when  both tests indicate um positive we have  a positive predictive value of 89  percent  almost 90 percent making it the highest  positive predictive testing on the  market  when both tests are negative indicating  immune quiescence and no injury we have  a 94 negative predictive value so when  we think about what this is done and  what this is doing for our patients our  clinicians and getting us out there is  that by combining the test we have  created something that has a high  positive and a high negative predictive  value but importantly this  this change was facilitated by getting  away from the lack of sensitivity that  we found in microarray and onto a more  sensitive more technologically advanced  solution with the biomark hd  so now we offer this as a single six mil  routine blood draw so previously you had  to have three different tubes to be able  to draw multiple tests and now we've  simplified this to one simple blood draw  that can be done in a normal of  different ways and also  no special packaging that comes with it  no cold packs no shipping it frozen or  anything like that with high level of  stability that comes with that secondary  to that of course is one easy to  interpret longitudinal report that is  showing you what is happening both for  true graph and track over the course of  time and hopefully providing more  granular detail for the patients and  clinicians to better gauge the health of  the kidney overall  so again combining these tests i think  the biggest thing that i would say is  that by looking at gene expression or  looking at cell free dna alone true  graph or track you are not giving full  coverage of potential rejections on both  sides here so by combining this test and  offering this we provide the value of  offering two tests um and one two one  report that has been really really  important in navigating this uh moving  forward so with that i appreciate your  time and i'm happy to answer any  questions that you may have  you

